{"Setting a missing refresh_token to the literal string \"refresh_token\" can overwrite a previously valid refresh token when callers merge/store .data, which would break subsequent refreshes": 0.8527929782867432, "minimumTokenResponseSchema uses computed keys ([z.string().toString()]), which will literally create keys like \"[object Object]\" and won't validate arbitrary numeric expiry fields as intended; safeParse will likely fail for real token responses": 0.9497809410095215, "parseRefreshTokenResponse returns a Zod safeParse result object, so data: { key } would persist { success, data, ... } instead of the credential JSON payload": 0.9730986952781677, "refreshOAuthTokens returns a fetch Response when syncing is enabled but returns whatever refreshFunction() returns otherwise (axios/hubspot/google responses), so downstream code can break depending on env": 0.955452561378479, "res?.data assumes a Gaxios-style response, but when refreshOAuthTokens uses fetch it returns a Response without .data, so token.access_token/token.expiry_date will be undefined and refresh will fail": 0.9712836742401123, "refreshOAuthTokens's third argument is userId, but this call passes credentialId; if syncing is enabled it will POST the wrong calcomUserId and likely refresh the wrong account": 0.9916998744010925, "After refreshing and storing the new Salesforce access token, the jsforce.Connection is still initialized from the pre-refresh credentialKey values, so immediate API calls may use an expired token": 0.9270576238632202, "appCredentialWebhookRequestBodySchema.parse (and the subsequent JSON.parse) can throw and return a 500 for malformed requests; without a method guard this endpoint is also callable via non-POST methods": 0.9542770981788635, "APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED resolves to a string/undefined (due to &&), not a boolean; any code that expects a strict boolean may behave unexpectedly": 0.8338992595672607}